vering Elements from K Lists', 'Heap', 'Hard', 'https://leetcode.com/problems/smallest-range-covering-elements-from-k-lists', 40, FALSE, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-13T08:21:21.439Z', NULL, FALSE, NULL, NULL), ('mla-1-1-1', 'user-default', 'goal-aws', 'Skill 1.1.1: Extract data from data sources (for example, Amazon S3, Amazon EBS, Amazon EFS, Amazon RDS, Amazon DynamoDB, Amazon OpenSearch Service).', 'Domain 1: Data Preparation for ML & AI', 'Hard', 'https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-access-training-data.html', 25, FALSE, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-14T14:47:00.125Z', 'Task 1.1: Collect and store data', TRUE, 'Skill 1.1.1 evaluates your ability to: ''Extract data from data sources (for example, Amazon S3, Amazon EBS, Amazon EFS, Amazon RDS, Amazon DynamoDB, Amazon OpenSearch Service).''. Within Task 1.1: Collect and store data under Domain 1: Data Preparation for ML & AI, this skill ensures that ML workloads maintain data integrity, optimal throughput, low latency, and robust fault-tolerance. As an AWS Machine Learning Engineer, you must know which managed services to select, how they connect, and how to eliminate performance bottlenecks.', 'Exam Tip: Use FSx for Lustre (linked to S3) for GPU training data caching; use S3 + Lake Formation for centralized data lake governance. Gotcha: Choosing EFS over FSx for Lustre for distributed multi-GPU training. EFS lacks the sub-millisecond Lustre parallel POSIX throughput needed to feed GPUs at 100Gbps.'), ('mla-1-1-2', 'user-default', 'goal-aws', 'Skill 1.1.2: Make storage decisions and conﬁgure storage services based on cost, performance, data structure, and data compliance.', 'Domain 1: Data Preparation for ML & AI', 'Hard', 'https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-access-training-data.html', 25, FALSE, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-14T14:47:00.125Z', 'Task 1.1: Collect and store data', TRUE, 'Skill 1.1.2 evaluates your ability to: ''Make storage decisions and conﬁgure storage services based on cost, performance, data structure, and data compliance.''. Within Task 1.1: Collect and store data under Domain 1: Data Preparation for ML & AI, this skill ensures that ML workloads maintain data integrity, optimal throughput, low latency, and robust fault-tolerance. As an AWS Machine Learning Engineer, you must know which managed services to select, how they connect, and how to eliminate performance bottlenecks.', 'Exam Tip: Use FSx for Lustre (linked to S3) for GPU training data caching; use S3 + Lake Formation for centralized data lake governance. Gotcha: Choosing EFS over FSx for Lustre for distributed multi-GPU training. EFS lacks the sub-millisecond Lustre parallel POSIX throughput needed to feed GPUs at 100Gbps.'), ('mla-1-1-3', 'user-default', 'goal-aws', 'Skill 1.1.3: Troubleshoot and debug data ingestion and storage issues that involve capacity and scalability.', 'Domain 1: Data Preparation for ML & AI', 'Medium', 'https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-access-training-data.html', 20, FALSE, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-14T14:47:00.125Z', 'Task 1.1: Collect and store data', FALSE, 'Skill 1.1.3 evaluates your ability to: ''Troubleshoot and debug data ingestion and storage issues that involve capacity and scalability.''. Within Task 1.1: Collect and store data under Domain 1: Data Preparation for ML & AI, this skill ensures that ML workloads maintain data integrity, optimal throughput, low latency, and robust fault-tolerance. As an AWS Machine Learning Engineer, you must know which managed services to select, how they connect, and how to eliminate performance bottlenecks.', 'Exam Tip: Use FSx for Lustre (linked to S3) for GPU training data caching; use S3 + Lake Formation for centralized data lake governance. Gotcha: Choosing EFS over FSx for Lustre for distributed multi-GPU training. EFS lacks the sub-millisecond Lustre parallel POSIX throughput needed to feed GPUs at 100Gbps.'), ('mla-1-1-4', 'user-default', 'goal-aws', 'Skill 1.1.4: Use AWS streaming data sources