ghput, low latency, and robust fault-tolerance. As an AWS Machine Learning Engineer, you must know which managed services to select, how they connect, and how to eliminate performance bottlenecks.', 'Exam Tip: Use FSx for Lustre (linked to S3) for GPU training data caching; use S3 + Lake Formation for centralized data lake governance. Gotcha: Choosing EFS over FSx for Lustre for distributed multi-GPU training. EFS lacks the sub-millisecond Lustre parallel POSIX throughput needed to feed GPUs at 100Gbps.'), ('mla-1-1-9', 'user-default', 'goal-aws', 'Skill 1.1.9: Ingest data into SageMaker Feature Store.', 'Domain 1: Data Preparation for ML & AI', 'Hard', 'https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-access-training-data.html', 25, FALSE, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-14T14:47:00.125Z', 'Task 1.1: Collect and store data', TRUE, 'Skill 1.1.9 evaluates your ability to: ''Ingest data into SageMaker Feature Store.''. Within Task 1.1: Collect and store data under Domain 1: Data Preparation for ML & AI, this skill ensures that ML workloads maintain data integrity, optimal throughput, low latency, and robust fault-tolerance. As an AWS Machine Learning Engineer, you must know which managed services to select, how they connect, and how to eliminate performance bottlenecks.', 'Exam Tip: Use FSx for Lustre (linked to S3) for GPU training data caching; use S3 + Lake Formation for centralized data lake governance. Gotcha: Choosing EFS over FSx for Lustre for distributed multi-GPU training. EFS lacks the sub-millisecond Lustre parallel POSIX throughput needed to feed GPUs at 100Gbps.'), ('mla-1-2-1', 'user-default', 'goal-aws', 'Skill 1.2.1: Transform data by using AWS tools (for example, AWS Glue, AWS Glue DataBrew, Spark on Amazon EMR, SageMaker Data Wrangler).', 'Domain 1: Data Preparation for ML & AI', 'Hard', 'https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/data-wrangler.html', 25, FALSE, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-14T14:47:00.125Z', 'Task 1.2: Perform data transformation, feature engineering, and pre-processing', TRUE, 'Skill 1.2.1 evaluates your ability to: ''Transform data by using AWS tools (for example, AWS Glue, AWS Glue DataBrew, Spark on Amazon EMR, SageMaker Data Wrangler).''. Within Task 1.2: Perform data transformation, feature engineering, and pre-processing under Domain 1: Data Preparation for ML & AI, this skill ensures that ML workloads maintain data integrity, optimal throughput, low latency, and robust fault-tolerance. As an AWS Machine Learning Engineer, you must know which managed services to select, how they connect, and how to eliminate performance bottlenecks.', 'Exam Tip: Store real-time feature lookups in Online Feature Store (DynamoDB backed, <10ms); batch features in Offline Store (S3 Parquet); use Data Wrangler for visual transformations that export directly to PySpark. Gotcha: Using SageMaker Feature Store Online Store for offline historical model training. The Online Store is backed by DynamoDB for ultra-low latency single-record lookups; use the Offline Store (S3 Parquet) for bulk training data extraction.'), ('mla-1-2-2', 'user-default', 'goal-aws', 'Skill 1.2.2: Create and manage features by using AWS tools (for example, SageMaker Feature Store).', 'Domain 1: Data Preparation for ML & AI', 'Hard', 'https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/data-wrangler.html', 25, FALSE, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-14T14:47:00.125Z', 'Task 1.2: Perform data transformation, feature engineering, and pre-processing', TRUE, 'Skill 1.2.2 evaluates your ability to: ''Create and manage features by using AWS tools (for example, SageMaker Feature Store).''. Within Task 1.2: Perform data transformation, feature engineering, and pre-processing under Domain 1: Data Preparation for ML & AI, this skill ensures that ML workloads maintain data integrity, optimal throughput, low latency, and robust fault-tolerance. As an AWS Machine Learning Engineer, you must know which managed services to select, how they connect, and how to eliminate performan