VALUES ('mla-3-1-5', 'user-default', 'goal-aws', 'Skill 3.1.5: Deploy models that were built outside of AWS into AWS environments (for example, Amazon SageMaker AI, Amazon Bedrock Custom Model Import).', 'Domain 3: Deployment & Orchestration of ML & AI Workflows', 'Medium', 'https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/realtime-endpoints.html', 20, FALSE, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-14T14:47:00.125Z', 'Task 3.1: Manage deployment infrastructure for ML and AI model types', FALSE, 'Skill 3.1.5 evaluates your ability to: ''Deploy models that were built outside of AWS into AWS environments (for example, Amazon SageMaker AI, Amazon Bedrock Custom Model Import).''. Within Task 3.1: Manage deployment infrastructure for ML and AI model types under Domain 3: Deployment & Orchestration of ML & AI Workflows, this skill ensures that ML workloads maintain data integrity, optimal throughput, low latency, and robust fault-tolerance. As an AWS Machine Learning Engineer, you must know which managed services to select, how they connect, and how to eliminate performance bottlenecks.', 'Exam Tip: Real-time (<10ms, steady traffic); Serverless (spiky/infrequent, zero-cost idle); Asynchronous (large payloads up to 1GB, long runtimes, S3 queuing); Batch Transform (bulk offline datasets). Gotcha: Using Real-Time Endpoints for large payload inputs (>6MB) or long-running inferences (>60s). Real-time endpoints time out at 60 seconds and max 6MB payload; use Asynchronous Endpoints (up to 1GB payload, 1-hour processing).'), ('mla-3-1-6', 'user-default', 'goal-aws', 'Skill 3.1.6: Deploy and conﬁgure agents for speciﬁc tasks, integration with other services and tools, and agent communication protocols.', 'Domain 3: Deployment & Orchestration of ML & AI Workflows', 'Hard', 'https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/realtime-endpoints.html', 25, FALSE, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-14T14:47:00.125Z', 'Task 3.1: Manage deployment infrastructure for ML and AI model types', TRUE, 'Skill 3.1.6 evaluates your a