VALUES ('mla-3-3-11', 'user-default', 'goal-aws', 'Skill 3.3.11: Conﬁgure AI-speciﬁc pipeline orchestration for RAG system updates and knowledge base refresh cycles.', 'Domain 3: Deployment & Orchestration of ML & AI Workflows', 'Hard', 'https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/pipelines.html', 25, FALSE, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-14T14:47:00.125Z', 'Task 3.3: Implement automated orchestration and continuous CI/CD pipelines', TRUE, 'Skill 3.3.11 evaluates your ability to: ''Conﬁgure AI-speciﬁc pipeline orchestration for RAG system updates and knowledge base refresh cycles.''. Within Task 3.3: Implement automated orchestration and continuous CI/CD pipelines under Domain 3: Deployment & Orchestration of ML & AI Workflows, this skill ensures that ML workloads maintain data integrity, optimal throughput, low latency, and robust fault-tolerance. As an AWS Machine Learning Engineer, you must know which managed services to select, how they connect, and how to eliminate performance bottlenecks.', 'Exam Tip: Define end-to-end DAG workflows in SageMaker Pipelines; gate deployments via SageMaker Model Registry approval states; automate deployment execution using EventBridge and CodePipeline. Gotcha: Triggering production deployment without an approved model status in SageMaker Model Registry. The exam requires Model Registry approval status transitions (`Approved`) to emit EventBridge events that trigger CI/CD deployment pipelines.'), ('mla-4-1-1', 'user-default', 'goal-aws', 'Skill 4.1.1: Monitor model performance in production by using Amazon CloudWatch generative AI observability, Amazon Bedrock Model Evaluation, and drift detection pipelines.', 'Domain 4: Operating, Monitoring & Securing ML & AI Solutions', 'Hard', 'https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor-data-quality.html', 25, FALSE, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-14T14:47:00.125Z', 'Task 4.1: Monitor ML and AI model inference and performance', TRUE, 'Skill 4.1.1 evaluates your ability to: ''Monitor model p